 "intro_html": "A festive noodle dish: chewy <b>sweet potato glass noodles</b> tossed with separately cooked vegetables and strips of egg, dressed in soy, sugar and plenty of sesame oil. Each vegetable is cooked on its own for a minute or two so it keeps its colour and texture; in a steel pan they go one after another without washing up in between. Beef is optional. This is a home adaptation built from several Korean sources and has not been kitchen tested.",
